::  name       comlink ipv6 dual stack
::  shape      families - int (@u32)
::  invariant  the dual-stack policy names exactly two address families (four bytes and sixteen bytes); bind never dial; sibling records never a union; any later family-choice wait is named and bounded (family_wait_ms=250)
::  example    2
::  readers    Comlink · Glow Tend R1 · Sur museum · Ashvini
::  nib        equinox-e221-comlink-r1-v1
::
::  Ashvini R1 · the remoting vane's first pedestal — a POLICY named, never a
::  wire changed. comlink/hosted_wire.rye speaks one family today; the policy
::  says a lawful host offers two, so the elder wire keeps its exact meaning
::  while the second family stands beside it. Bind, never dial. No datagram
::  field, no nonce, no sealing touched by this seat.
::  Sibling address lengths (named, not braided): ipv4_addr_len=4 ·
::  ipv6_addr_len=16. Happy-eyeballs family wait ceiling: 250 ms.
::  Ruling: counsel/20260802-163000_e219-comlink-module-seam-ruling.md
::  Counsel cut: counsel/20260802-164500_e220-r1-dual-stack-cut.md
+$  comlink-ipv6-dual-stack-shape
